Load libGL.so, libGLU.so... by their file names on illumos as on Linux.

On anything but Linux, PyOpenGL falls back to ctypes.util.find_library(),
which returns None for "GL" on illumos, so "import OpenGL.GL" fails with
"Unable to load OpenGL library".  The Linux code path (libGL.so, then libGL.so.N) works.

https://github.com/mcfletch/pyopengl/pull/179

--- pyopengl-3.1.10/OpenGL/platform/ctypesloader.py.orig
+++ pyopengl-3.1.10/OpenGL/platform/ctypesloader.py
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@
     """
     if isinstance( dllType, ctypes.LibraryLoader ):
         dllType = dllType._dlltype
-    if sys.platform.startswith('linux'):
+    if sys.platform.startswith(('linux', 'sunos')):
         return _loadLibraryPosix(dllType, name, mode)
     else:
         return _loadLibraryWindows(dllType, name, mode)
